{"slug":"hold-btc-while-stablecoin-supply-grows","name":"Hold BTC while stablecoin supply grows","status":"rejected","created_at":"2026-11-15T05:59:45.402270Z","version":1,"frozen":true,"implementation":"stablecoin-hold","runs":2,"trials":2,"deflated_sharpe":2.2915562956749014e-05,"asset_class":"crypto","sections":{"hypothesis":"Hypothesis","rationale":"Why the edge should exist","rules":"Rules in plain English","falsification":"What would prove it wrong","parameters":"Parameters and allowed ranges","costs":"Expected turnover against costs"},"notes":[{"version":1,"created_at":"2026-11-15T05:59:45.402270Z","sections":{"hypothesis":"Holding BTC only in weeks that start after 4 weeks of stablecoin supply growth, and cash otherwise, beats holding BTC at the same average exposure on Sharpe, after costs.","rationale":"The raw-effect study (note does-stablecoin-supply-growth-lead-prices, 2026-11-15) found weeks after supply growth averaged +0.78% against -0.38% after shrinkage on BTC and ETH pooled (PROCEED, P 91%), with little overlap with momentum. Who pays: new dollars enter crypto as stablecoins before they buy coins, so supply growth is fresh demand arriving. This trades exactly what was measured. It also settles the study's weak spot: pooling BTC and ETH weeks overstated its confidence, and a BTC-only run tests the effect on one coin with its own Sharpe and confidence interval. Not a variant of a rejected family (it reads money flows, not prices or sentiment). Unlike the rotation variants, its holdout year is unseen for this signal: the supply's path in 2025-26 hasn't been looked at, so a pass here could go on to the holdout.","rules":"stablecoin-hold on BTCUSDT daily bars: at each Sunday close (UTC), hold BTC for the next week if stablecoins_up is 1 (the supply known at the close, counted from two days after each day, above its value 28 days before), else cash; unknown is cash. Fills at Monday's open, 330 USDT, costs from kestrel.toml (7.5 bps fees with the BNB discount). Period 2018-01 to 2025-10, before the holdout. Also run on ETHUSDT with the same rule, reported separately.","falsification":"The full scorecard on BTC: fails on any failed test (random entry n/a: it holds weights). ETH is reported beside it and must not contradict it badly (a Sharpe below ETH held at the same exposure is noted as a warning, not a separate pass). A pass leads to a holdout note; a fail ends the idea.","parameters":"None to choose: 28 days, the two-day lag and Sunday decisions are fixed by the study. Robustness is n/a (no settings), as for weekly momentum.","costs":"A switch at most weekly; the study's split (602 growing weeks, 214 shrinking) suggests perhaps 15-30 switches a year, about 0.3-0.5% a year at 17 bps a round trip. Trials: 2 runs (BTC, ETH)."},"implementation":"stablecoin-hold","frozen_at":"2026-11-15T06:00:19.617802Z","change_reason":null}],"history":[{"status":"idea","at":"2026-11-15T05:59:45.402270Z","reason":"Created"},{"status":"specified","at":"2026-11-15T06:00:19.617828Z","reason":"v1 frozen"},{"status":"backtested","at":"2026-11-15T06:01:53.224008Z","reason":"first run on v1"},{"status":"rejected","at":"2026-11-15T06:06:02.022869Z","reason":"Failed the scorecard (Luke, 2026-11-15): beat holding at the same exposure on BTC (0.81 vs 0.74) and ETH (0.75 vs 0.68), but failed walk-forward (4 and 5 of 11), start dates, trades (27 of 30), drawdown (-66%, -80%) and luck (6%, 4%). Kept on watch."}],"trial_log":[{"id":"20261115-060153-5833e3","created_at":"2026-11-15T06:01:53.219188Z","strategy":"stablecoin-hold","strategy_kind":"research","style":"weights","engine":"event","params":{},"research":{"slug":"hold-btc-while-stablecoin-supply-grows","version":1},"strategy_name":"hold while stablecoins grow BTCUSDT","symbol":"BTCUSDT","benchmark_symbol":"BTCUSDT","universe_coins":null,"forced_exits":0,"deflated_sharpe":2.2915562956749014e-05,"deflated_trials":883,"interval":"1d","start":"2018-01","end":"2025-10","scored_from":null,"history_